 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T06:44:21-08:00","id":1272377,"title":"","content":"Biggest thing I see are interaction rules. Like not having opposable thumbs, needing water to breathe, people not talking to (Politics and Streetwise) a talking boa constrictor, etc.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Attributes and such should be easy enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T10:25:08-08:00","id":1272412,"title":"","content":"Primarily I'm interested in understanding if there is already something out there for this, independently or in one of the game lines. I may be dreaming that I read something on the subject here before.<br /> <br /> That said, uplifting an animal wouldn't be too hard if we were to define a set of merits that accomplishes the step-up in intelligence and capabilities (speaking, say). Animals, for example, have mental stats but the don't work on quite the same scale. Certain magics (Mind, Life, other sorcerous modifications) could do this easily. I'm not really thinking &quot;add opposable thumbs&quot; as that crosses the line into hybrid in my book.<br /> <br /> I got on this track of thinking by conceiving an scenario for a PC who might be able to turn his soul/spirit into a raven to escape what would otherwise be certain death. And then, probably would not be able to turn back. (Long story, so just roll with this.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T10:54:15-08:00","id":1272424,"title":"","content":"We say her <b>Pugmire</b> and <b>Mau</b> uplifting of animals were they have more or less human features? Or just that animal stays totally in it's form, it just can think and speak like humans?<br /> <br /> <b>Pugmire</b> and <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> Uplifting<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px 